# CPython 3.11 and its extension modules retain interpreter-global state even
# after the sanitizer-only CTest build calls Py_FinalizeEx at executable exit.
# The runner's full 64-frame traces show those remaining allocations originate
# in libpython, NumPy, or SciPy rather than Fullseye's native ownership tables.
#
# CPython 3.11 と拡張モジュールは、sanitizer 専用 CTest build が実行ファイル終了時に
# Py_FinalizeEx を呼んだ後にも、解釈系全体の状態を残す。runner で 64 frame を採った
# 結果、残る確保は Fullseye の native 所有表でなく libpython、NumPy、SciPy に由来する。
#
# This intentionally matches libpython3 only, and only the ASan CI job loads
# this file.  It can hide a missing Fullseye DECREF when that allocation was
# made inside CPython, so tests/test_c_api_pybind11.py repeats the same released
# C-API threshold call 1,000 times and checks that sys.getallocatedblocks does
# not keep increasing. Native allocations whose stack never enters libpython
# remain visible to LSan.
#
# libpython3 だけに当て、読み込むのは ASan CI job に限る。ただし CPython 内部で確保した
# Fullseye の DECREF 漏れも隠れ得るため、tests/test_c_api_pybind11.py は同じ C API の
# threshold 呼出しを解放つきで 1,000 回繰り返し、sys.getallocatedblocks が増え続けない
# ことを確認する。stack が libpython に入らない native 確保は LSan に残る。
leak:libpython3
